T63	Quotation 14318 14337	"Such sweet lines!"
T64	Cue 14338 14347	continued
T65	Entity 14348 14355	Harriet
T66	Quotation 14358 14504	"these two last!-- But how shall I ever be able to return the paper, or say I have found it out?-- Oh! Miss Woodhouse, what can we do about that?"
R79	Cueing Arg1:T64 Arg2:T63	
R80	Cueing Arg1:T64 Arg2:T66	
R81	Speaker Arg1:T65 Arg2:T63	
R82	Speaker Arg1:T65 Arg2:T66	
T67	Quotation 14505 14768	"Leave it to me.  You do nothing.  He will be here this evening, I dare say, and then I will give it him back, and some nonsense or other will pass between us, and you shall not be committed.-- Your soft eyes shall chuse their own time for beaming.  Trust to me."
R83	Speaker Arg1:T54 Arg2:T67	
R84	Addressee Arg1:T65 Arg2:T67	
T68	Quotation 14769 14904	"Oh! Miss Woodhouse, what a pity that I must not write this beautiful charade into my book! I am sure I have not got one half so good."
R85	Speaker Arg1:T65 Arg2:T68	
R86	Addressee Arg1:T54 Arg2:T68	
T69	Quotation 14905 15003	"Leave out the two last lines, and there is no reason why you should not write it into your book."
R87	Speaker Arg1:T54 Arg2:T69	
R88	Addressee Arg1:T65 Arg2:T69	
T70	Quotation 15004 15033	"Oh! but those two lines are"
R89	Addressee Arg1:T54 Arg2:T70	
R90	Speaker Arg1:T65 Arg2:T70	
T71	Quotation 15038 15636	"The best of all.  Granted;-- for private enjoyment; and for private enjoyment keep them.  They are not at all the less written you know, because you divide them.  The couplet does not cease to be, nor does its meaning change.  But take it away, and all appropriation ceases, and a very pretty gallant charade remains, fit for any collection. Depend upon it, he would not like to have his charade slighted, much better than his passion.  A poet in love must be encouraged in both capacities, or neither.  Give me the book, I will write it down, and then there can be no possible reflection on you."
R91	Speaker Arg1:T54 Arg2:T71	
R92	Addressee Arg1:T65 Arg2:T71	
T72	Quotation 15856 15909	"I shall never let that book go out of my own hands,"
T73	Cue 15910 15914	said
T74	Entity 15915 15918	she
R93	Cueing Arg1:T73 Arg2:T72	
R94	Speaker Arg1:T74 Arg2:T72	
